[
  {
    "file": "web/src/screens/MyProfileScreen.tsx",
    "line": 44,
    "summary": "Violates the CLAUDE.md frontend rule 'Handle loading / empty / error / success states': the skills-taxonomy query (`skillsQuery`) has no isError/isPending handling anywhere in this file — `const skills = skillsQuery.data ?? [];` (line 174) silently falls back to an empty array on failure, unlike every other query in this same file (profileQuery, availabilityQuery) and unlike the identical `useQuery({queryKey: [\"skills\"], ...})` in web/src/screens/SkillsScreen.tsx (line 44 there), which does add `skillsQuery.isError && <ErrorBanner .../>` and `skillsQuery.isPending` skeleton states.",
    "failure_scenario": "If GET /skills fails (network blip, 500, org has zero skills configured), the 'Add a skill' form section on My Profile just disappears with zero explanation (it's gated by `availableToAdd.length > 0`, which is empty on fetch failure) — a crew member sees no error, no retry button, and no way to tell 'the request failed' apart from 'you already hold every skill in the org.' The exact same failure mode was already solved correctly one file over (SkillsScreen.tsx), so this is a real regression in consistency, not a missing feature."
  }
]

